    "short_description": "Document an ancient paradise before it's lost forever. Study the behaviour of the EMUUROM creatures and use the gained knowledge to create new paths forward. Slowly, the machinations of the mythic forest sprites begin to unfold.",
    "supported_languages": "English",
    "reviews": "\u201cit's literally for the people who go into the journal feature of creatures in games and just spend hours there\u201d<br>CheshireCreeper<br><br>\u201cEmuurom brought me back to the golden age of indie Flash games \u2013 it's a beautifully crafted, creative, exploration-focused experience full of secrets and cozy feelings.\u201d<br>5/5 \u2013 Samuel \u201cobskyr\u201d Messner<br><br>\u201cThe energy of the game is certainly different from other titles. Cozier and inquisitive, it appeals to a more academic mindset that adores the surprise that video games can deliver. It\u2019s a medium that can be anything that you can possibly fathom. Emuurom embodies this at its core\u201d<br>The Visualist's Veranda<br>",
